# MotoRoute — Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## 1. Product Vision
MotoRoute is an iOS community app for motorcycle riders to plan rides, save them for later, and share verified routes they have actually ridden. Instead of relying on generic point-to-point directions, riders discover routes vetted by other motorcyclists—complete with real photos, road conditions, stops, and star ratings.

**Core Loop:**
**Plan** a route → **Ride** it → Get **Reminded** → **Publish** with photos & tips → **Discover** & rate other rides.

---

## 2. Target Audience
- Everyday and weekend motorcycle riders who want to discover scenic, twisty, or reliable routes near them.
- Riders who already use Google Maps to plan or navigate, but want a dedicated place to save, organize, and share their favorite rides with the community.

---

## 3. Core Features & Screens

### 3.1 Login & Onboarding
- Riders sign in quickly using their **Google account** (with **Apple Sign-In** alongside it for iOS).
- On first login, their basic profile (name and photo) is set up automatically so they can jump straight into the feed.

### 3.2 Explore Feed (Home)
The main screen where riders discover published routes.
- **Two Feed Views:**
  - **Nearby:** Shows rides closest to the rider's current area.
  - **Popular:** Shows the highest-rated and most-reviewed rides.
- **Ride Card Layout:**
  - **Top:** A clean map preview showing the route path, with a small badge indicating the ride's difficulty (e.g., *Beginner*, *Intermediate*, *Technical*).
  - **Bottom:** Ride title, starting area, highlighted stats (distance and estimated ride time), and the average star rating with review count (e.g., `★ 4.8 (24)`).

### 3.3 Plan a Ride (Private Drafts)
Allows riders to map out a future trip before they hit the road.
- **Route Builder:** Pick a starting point (Point A), add optional stops (gas stations, diners, viewpoints), and pick a destination (Point B).
- **Details:** Give the ride a title and optionally set a **Planned Ride Date**.
- **Reminder Toggle:** Option to turn on *"Remind me to publish after the ride."*
- **Two Ways to Save:**
  - **Save as Planned Ride:** Keeps the route private in the rider's profile so they can use it when ride day arrives.
  - **Publish Now:** For riders who are recreating a favorite route they have already ridden and want to share immediately.

### 3.4 Post-Ride Reminder Notification
- If a rider saves a Planned Ride with a date, the app sends a friendly reminder after the ride date: *"Hey, how was [Ride Title]? Don't forget to publish your ride!"*
- Tapping the notification opens the ride directly to the **Publish** flow.

### 3.5 "I Rode This" Publish Flow
A fast, under-60-second checklist to turn a Planned Ride into a public recommendation:
1. **Add Photos:** Upload up to 5 photos from the trip.
2. **Quick-Tap Tags:**
   - **Difficulty:** Beginner / Intermediate / Technical
   - **Road Surface:** Paved / Mix / Gravel
   - **Vibe & Alerts:** Scenic, Twisty, Chill, Good Food, Potholes, No Gas Stations.
3. **Rider Notes + AI Polish:** A short text box (*"Any tips for other riders?"*) with an optional **"Enhance with AI"** button that turns the stops, stats, tags, and quick notes into a clean, readable route description.
4. **Publish:** Moves the ride from private to the public Explore Feed.

### 3.6 Ride Detail & Reviews
The full view when a rider taps any card.
- **Interactive Map:** Zoomable map showing the full route and stops, with a prominent **"Open in Google Maps"** button so the rider can immediately navigate it.
- **Ride Info:** Title, author's name and motorcycle model, key stats (distance, time, difficulty, surface), photo gallery, and route description.
- **If Viewing Your Own Planned Ride:** Shows a clear **"I Rode This — Publish"** button.
- **Ratings & Reviews (Published Rides):** Riders can leave a **1–5 star rating** and an optional comment (e.g., road hazards, best time of day to go, food recommendations).

### 3.7 Rider Profile
- **Basic Info:** Profile photo, display name, and a short bio.
- **My Garage:** Details about their motorcycle (Make, Model, Year, and Bike Type—e.g., *Sport, Cruiser, Adventure, Naked*).
- **My Rides (Two Tabs):**
  - **Published Rides:** Public routes they have shared.
  - **Planned Rides:** Private drafts they haven't ridden yet.

---

## 4. Navigation Structure
Simple 3-tab bottom bar:
1. **Explore** (Feed)
2. **+ Plan** (Create a new route)
3. **Profile** (Garage + Published & Planned rides)

---

## 5. Community Safety & Trust
- Riders can **report** any inappropriate ride or review.
- Riders can **block** other users.
- Riders can **delete their account** and associated data from Profile Settings.

---

## 6. Out of Scope (Not in Version 1)
To keep the first version focused and fast to launch, the following are intentionally excluded:
- Built-in turn-by-turn voice navigation (riders hand off to Google Maps).
- Live background GPS ride recording.
- Group ride scheduling, RSVPs, or in-app chat.
